This is granite, so it falls in heading 6802 (worked monumental or building stone). Polished slabs of granite are classified in 6802.93 ("Granite: other"). Subheading 6802.93.00 covers "Other: Granite", and the 10-digit statistical suffixes are 6802.93.0010 (Slabs, 2 or more cm thick?) Let me recall. 6802.93.00 has these statistical suffixes: 10 "Slabs" and 90 "Other." Actually, I recall 6802.93.0010 as "Slabs" and 6802.93.0090 as "Other." Slabs as such are imported for further cutting, which fits here.

There is also a split by thickness. 6802.93.00 splits into 6802.93.0010 (Slabs: 2 cm or more... ) Not sure, but I will go with 6802.93.0010. The 6802.23 subheading is for granite worked simply cut or sawn with a flat or even surface. The polished and beveled stone goes beyond that, so 6802.93 is right. 6802.93.00 is "Granite: Other," and a 6802.93.0010 "Slabs" suffix is plausible.

